Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 10:28:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] ImsService: Always use +EIREG for IMS registration updates

ImsService only trusts +EIREG for registration updates when the
mtkradioex HAL is 4.1 or newer. Our vendor RIL exposes the HIDL
mtkradioex@3.0 interface, so +EIREG is ignored and the IMS
registration tech is never updated on LTE <-> Wi-Fi handover,
leaving the framework thinking IMS is registered over LTE while
VoWiFi is in use.

Drop the HAL version check so mNotifyUseEireg is set whenever an
+EIREG indication arrives.
---
 smali/com/mediatek/ims/ImsService$MyHandler.smali | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/smali/com/mediatek/ims/ImsService$MyHandler.smali b/smali/com/mediatek/ims/ImsService$MyHandler.smali
index fc831e6..a8c45b8 100644
--- a/smali/com/mediatek/ims/ImsService$MyHandler.smali
+++ b/smali/com/mediatek/ims/ImsService$MyHandler.smali
@@ -3668,8 +3668,6 @@
 
     move-result v11
 
-    if-eqz v11, :cond_28
-
     .line 3100
     iget-object v11, v1, Lcom/mediatek/ims/ImsService$MyHandler;->this$0:Lcom/mediatek/ims/ImsService;
 
